welcome back to las vegas now it's the  season of giving so it's the perfect  time to support children in our  community through the las vegas rotary  club santa claus event here to tell us  more about the upcoming event is the las  vegas rotary club santa claus program  organizer michael gordon hi michael hi  jillian how are you good thank you so  much for being here we were talking a  little bit off-camera this is such a  cool event and you guys have been doing  it for a long time tell me all about it  yes so for this is our 26th annual santa  claus event so for the past 25 years  we've donated over 1.5 million in goods  and services to almost 6 000 kids in the  las vegas valley so we're so happy to  have it back the kids back this year  again because we know this is the time  of giving back yeah this is going to be  so special for them and what i love  about it is they get to actually come  and shop and pick out stuff how does it  all work yes so the kids show up we work  with 13 partner agencies agencies like  salvation army shade tree boys and girls  clubs they bring the kids to three  jcpenney's locations around the valley  and then the kids shop for coats shoes  socks shoes underwear  whatever they want because we want every  kid to leave with a new pair of clothes  that's so cool and we're seeing some  video from past years and the kids just  look so happy and they're having such a  special experience and in addition to  shopping you continue the day on and you  bring them over to unlv right yes our  club and i should say we use all the  clubs in the las vegas valley so we  believe in youth education and we want  them to experience the college  environment we know so many kids for  them it's first generation so they get  to interact with some of the unlv  athletes they render off some of that  energy that we get from the morning we  give them a lunch and then they hear an  inspirational talk about the importance  of education at unlv wow what a cool day  for them and this event is called santa  claus but santa claus makes an  appearance  yeah well  yes he shows up at the end we we cannot  do it without him and we cannot do it  without the support of the whole  community and if people want to get  involved where do they go or how can  they take part sure the las vegas  rotary.com and you just look for santa  claus there you can donate or if you  know of somebody who you think should  benefit  please reach out to that email address  or one of the partner agencies on your  website and the rotary club just does so  much in the community how special are  these events and to see everyone in the  community come together and support you  guys in everything that you do yes  rotary is a civic organization and we  are about to celebrate our centennial  next year in the valley so we've been  around for some time but we're not the  only club there's a bunch of clubs  around and we you know we care about the  youth and we want to help where we can  well thank you for all that you do and  we're going to help so many kids this  year and i can't believe 26th year we're  heading into  it's just gonna keep getting bigger and  better and i can't wait to see what you  guys do next so thank you so much  michael and for all the information of  how you can take part there's your  information on the screen december 2nd  for more information just go to las  vegasry.com  we'll be right back
 

